## Context
The ticket 0375 trial sweep (`docs/2026-10-09-t0375-project-rules-inventory.md`,
§ Non-writing rules) found about six project-local rules that are not about
writing, so they fall outside 0375's writing scope. They cover Python
(test tiers, data traps, JSON trailing newline), tickets (fast path,
ID-collision scan), workflow (science vs tooling lane, test one before
blasting, audit before instrumenting) and skills (prefer skills over commands).

## Actions
1. For each O row in the inventory, decide: promote to `rules/coding-python.md`,
   `tickets/AGENTS.md`, `rules/workflow.md` or `authoring-skills.md`; keep it
   local; or record it as memory.
2. Respect resident budgets: `workflow.md` is loaded every session.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Every O row has a recorded verdict
- [ ] Promoted rules land once, harness-level; project trims proposed per repo
- [ ] `make check` passes
